  <layout>One column of Greek verb forms with Latin equivalents in a narrow right margin; running head at top; signature "m 5" centred below the text.</layout>
  <page_number>185</page_number>
  <running_head>DE VERBO ACTIVO.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>m 5</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l>δεδώκαμεν δεδώκατε δεδώκασι.</l>
    <head level="3">Plusquamperfectum.</head>
    <l>ἐδεδώκειν ἐδεδώκεις ἐδεδώκει. <note side="right">Dederam</note></l>
    <l>ἐδεδώκειτον ἐδεδωκείτην</l>
    <l>ἐδεδώκειμεν ἐδεδώκειτε ἐδεδώκεισαν.</l>
    <head level="3">Infinitum α.</head>
    <l>ἔδωκα ἔδωκας ἔδωκε. <note side="right">Dedi.</note></l>
    <l>ἐδώκατον ἐδωκάτην</l>
    <l>ἐδώκαμεν ἐδώκατε ἔδωκαν.</l>
    <head level="3">Infinitum β.</head>
    <l>ἔδων ἔδως ἔδω. <note side="right">Dedi.</note></l>
    <l>ἔδοτον ἐδότην</l>
    <l>ἔδομεν ἔδοτε ἔδοσαν uel ἔδων</l>
    <head level="3">Futurum α.</head>
    <l>δώσω δώσεις δώσει. <note side="right">Dabo.</note></l>
    <l>δώσετον δώσετον</l>
    <l>δώσομεν δώσετε δώσουσι.</l>
    <head level="2">IMPERATIVUS.</head>
    <head level="3">Præsens.</head>
    <l>δίδοθι διδότω. <note side="right">Da.</note></l>
    <l>δίδοτον διδότων.</l>
    <l>δίδοτε διδότωσαν.</l>
    <head level="3">Perfectum.</head>
    <l>δέδωκε δεδωκέτω. <note side="right">Dato tu.</note></l>
    <l>δεδώκετον δεδωκέτων.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Greek forms are transcribed from a small, slightly worn print; accents on several forms (notably the Plusquamperfectum and Perfectum endings) are uncertain and may differ from the printed accents. The top line is partly cut at the head of the page. Right-margin notes are Latin equivalents: Dederam, Dedi. (twice), Dabo., Da., Dato tu.</notes>
</page>
